#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/cases/fullerene.ts:52
msgid "Each of the 30 icosahedron edges yields two truncation vertices, giving 60 atoms; the 12 original vertices become pentagons and the 20 triangular faces become hexagons. Each atom connects to three neighbors, giving 60 × 3 / 2 = 90 edges and 60 × 3 = 180 endpoint pairs, plus projected crossing pairs. Both front and back layers are retained; the rational approximation of the golden ratio affects only the shape, while the submitted rational coordinates and their intersections are still computed exactly."
msgstr "Each of the 30 icosahedron edges yields two truncation vertices, giving 60 atoms; the 12 original vertices become pentagons and the 20 triangular faces become hexagons. Each atom connects to three neighbors, giving 60 × 3 / 2 = 90 edges and 60 × 3 = 180 endpoint pairs, plus projected crossing pairs. Both front and back layers are retained; the rational approximation of the golden ratio affects only the shape, while the submitted rational coordinates and their intersections are still computed exactly."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/cases/presets.ts:38
msgid "Each of the 8 inner junctions joins 4 edges, each of the 8 outer junctions joins 3 edges, and the center joins 8 edges. There are 8 + 8 + 1 = 17 distinct intersection positions and 8 × 6 + 8 × 3 + 28 = 100 pairs. For example, four edges at (12, 0) produce 6 pairs, and three edges at (24, 0) produce 3 pairs. There are no crossings between rings and no overlapping edges."
msgstr "Each of the 8 inner junctions joins 4 edges, each of the 8 outer junctions joins 3 edges, and the center joins 8 edges. There are 8 + 8 + 1 = 17 distinct intersection positions and 8 × 6 + 8 × 3 + 28 = 100 pairs. For example, four edges at (12, 0) produce 6 pairs, and three edges at (24, 0) produce 3 pairs. There are no crossings between rings and no overlapping edges."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/cases/carbonLattices.ts:109
msgid "Each of the four centers has 4 spatial bonds of equal length, with pairwise direction dot products of −1 and squared lengths of 3, matching the tetrahedral angle. Six shared nearest neighbors have degree 2, and four boundary atoms have degree 1. The projection is (x + 3z/10, y + 7z/10); center (1,1,1) projects to (13/10,17/10), where four bonds produce 6 pairs. S6 and S13 cross internally at (281/100,489/100); a two-dimensional crossing is not an additional chemical bond, and the projection uses exact rational numbers."
msgstr "Each of the four centers has 4 spatial bonds of equal length, with pairwise direction dot products of −1 and squared lengths of 3, matching the tetrahedral angle. Six shared nearest neighbors have degree 2, and four boundary atoms have degree 1. The projection is (x + 3z/10, y + 7z/10); center (1,1,1) projects to (13/10,17/10), where four bonds produce 6 pairs. S6 and S13 cross internally at (281/100,489/100); a two-dimensional crossing is not an additional chemical bond, and the projection uses exact rational numbers."

