#: src/cases/penrose.ts:83
msgid "Subdivision uses φ = (1 + √5)/2. Matching Robinson triangles are paired along their bases and their internal diagonals removed; unpaired boundary halves are discarded, leaving 10 thin and 10 thick rhombi. The 50 unique edges connect 31 vertices: 5 have degree 2, 20 have degree 3, and 6 have degree 5, giving 5 × 1 + 20 × 3 + 6 × 10 = 125 endpoint pairs at 31 intersection positions; the origin joins 5 edges, giving exactly 10 pairs. Joins have no interior crossings or overlaps. Approximated shared vertices are uniformly rotated exactly by (x, y) → ((3x − 4y)/5, (4x + 3y)/5), preserving lengths, angles, and joins. The service computes the submitted rational coordinates exactly, without treating approximated rhombi as exact irrational geometry."
msgstr "Subdivision uses φ = (1 + √5)/2. Matching Robinson triangles are paired along their bases and their internal diagonals removed; unpaired boundary halves are discarded, leaving 10 thin and 10 thick rhombi. The 50 unique edges connect 31 vertices: 5 have degree 2, 20 have degree 3, and 6 have degree 5, giving 5 × 1 + 20 × 3 + 6 × 10 = 125 endpoint pairs at 31 intersection positions; the origin joins 5 edges, giving exactly 10 pairs. Joins have no interior crossings or overlaps. Approximated shared vertices are uniformly rotated exactly by (x, y) → ((3x − 4y)/5, (4x + 3y)/5), preserving lengths, angles, and joins. The service computes the submitted rational coordinates exactly, without treating approximated rhombi as exact irrational geometry."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/cases/carbonLattices.ts:118
msgid "The 36 interior atoms each have 3 bonds, while the 12 terminal atoms at the two openings each retain 1 bond; the degree sum is 36×3 + 12 = 120, giving 60 unique bonds. Circumferential indices connect modulo 6 without duplicating the seam; only axial boundaries are truncated. Cylinder coordinates and the fixed oblique projection are rounded to 1/10000, then rotated and uniformly scaled by 3/4; intersections are computed exactly for the actual rational inputs. For example, S1 and S19 cross internally at (1640458343/2867030000,-4910230279/11468120000); a projected crossing is not an atomic connection."
msgstr "The 36 interior atoms each have 3 bonds, while the 12 terminal atoms at the two openings each retain 1 bond; the degree sum is 36×3 + 12 = 120, giving 60 unique bonds. Circumferential indices connect modulo 6 without duplicating the seam; only axial boundaries are truncated. Cylinder coordinates and the fixed oblique projection are rounded to 1/10000, then rotated and uniformly scaled by 3/4; intersections are computed exactly for the actual rational inputs. For example, S1 and S19 cross internally at (1640458343/2867030000,-4910230279/11468120000); a projected crossing is not an atomic connection."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/cases/presets.ts:39
msgid "The center joins 6 main branches, producing 15 pairs; each main branch has two forks where four edges meet, producing 6 pairs per fork. There are 1 + 6 × 2 = 13 intersection positions and 15 + 12 × 6 = 87 pairs. For example, (3, 0) and (6, 0) each have 6 pairs; tips join only one edge and produce no pairs. There are no crossings or overlaps between forks. The ideal coordinates with sixfold symmetry use a fixed rational approximation."
msgstr "The center joins 6 main branches, producing 15 pairs; each main branch has two forks where four edges meet, producing 6 pairs per fork. There are 1 + 6 × 2 = 13 intersection positions and 15 + 12 × 6 = 87 pairs. For example, (3, 0) and (6, 0) each have 6 pairs; tips join only one edge and produce no pairs. There are no crossings or overlaps between forks. The ideal coordinates with sixfold symmetry use a fixed rational approximation."

